Regarding the code extension, you mentioned extending JavaScript code for user authentication with two-factor authentication (2FA) via email, but you did not provide the original code snippet. To help you effectively, I will provide a conceptual implementation of how to add 2FA via email to a standard Node.js/Express authentication flow. This example assumes you have a basic login route and a user model.

### Conceptual Implementation of 2FA via Email

This implementation adds a step after successful password verification where a 6-digit code is sent to the user's email. The user must then submit this code to complete authentication.

#### 1. Generate and Send 2FA Code (After Password Verification)

```javascript
const crypto = require('crypto');
const nodemailer = require('nodemailer');

// Mock function to send email (replace with your actual email service)
async function sendEmail(to, subject, text) {
    const transporter = nodemailer.createTransport({
        service: 'gmail',
        auth: {
            user: process.env.EMAIL_USER,
            pass: process.env.EMAIL_PASS
        }
    });

    await transporter.sendMail({
        from: process.env.EMAIL_USER,
        to: to,
        subject: subject,
        text: text
    });
}

// Helper to generate a 6-digit random code
function generateTwoFactorCode() {
    return crypto.randomInt(100000, 999999).toString();
}

